  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a graph with NNN vertices (numbered 111 to NNN) and MMM bidirectional edges, which doesn't contain multiple edges or self-loops — that is, the given graph is a simple undirected graph.\n\nFor each pair of vertices a,ba, ba,b such that 1≤a,b≤N1 \\leq a, b \\leq N1≤a,b≤N, it is possible to add a new edge between vertices aaa and bbb to the graph, with a cost of (a−b)2(a - b)^2(a−b)2.\n\nFind the minimum cost of adding edges so that vertex NNN is reachable from vertex 111.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 space-separated integers, NNN and MMM.\nThe ithi^{th}ith of the next MMM lines contains 222 space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting a bidirectional edge between vertex uiu_iui​ and vertex viv_ivi​ in the graph.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the answer in a single line.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤M≤2⋅1050 \\leq M \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^50≤M≤2⋅105",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The graph doesn't contain self-loops or multiple edges",
      "Sum of NNN over all testcases is no more than 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "Sum of MMM over all testcases is no more than 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 0\n5 4\n3 2\n1 4\n5 3\n4 2\n6 3\n1 2\n3 2\n1 3",
        "output": "1\n0\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: Add an edge between vertices 111 and 222, with cost (1−2)2=1(1-2)^2 = 1(1−2)2=1.\nTest Case 222: Vertices 111 and 555 are already connected, so no edges need to be added."
      }
    ]
